# Keys a terminal sends as bytes some other key is sent as too, so that what
# AmberEdit reads is that other key and can be nothing better. A line is the key,
# the bytes as a file under testdata/keys/ writes them, and what they are read as.
#
# Every line is a fact about a terminal, taken off a file beside this one. A key
# AmberEdit reads wrongly when the terminal sent something it could have told
# apart is a bug in ui/term/terminal.cpp, and goes there and not here.

# Ctrl with H, I, J and M is the C0 byte Backspace, Tab, Line Feed and Enter have
# been sent as since ASCII. Only the kitty keyboard protocol tells them apart, and
# only in the terminals that speak it.
Ctrl-H          \x08        Backspace
Ctrl-I          \x09        Tab
Ctrl-J          \x0a        Enter
Ctrl-M          \x0d        Enter

# Ctrl-Backspace is one of the two bytes Backspace itself is sent as, which of
# them being the terminal's choice; only the kitty protocol's CSI 127;5u is the
# chord. PuTTY sends Ctrl-Delete as the same 7FH.
Ctrl-Backspace  \x08        Backspace
Ctrl-Backspace  \x7f        Backspace
Ctrl-Del        \x7f        Backspace

# Shift-Space is a plain space wherever nothing has been asked to report it, and
# modifyOtherKeys at level 1 does not ask.
Shift-Space     \x20        Space

# WezTerm with enable_kitty_keyboard on sends a bare Delete as 08H under the
# kitty protocol, where the protocol says CSI 3 ~ — its own bug, and 08H is
# Backspace in half the terminals here.
Del             \x08        Backspace

# st sends Ctrl-Home and Alt-Delete as the bare keys.
Ctrl-Home       \e[1~       Home
Alt-Del         \e[3~       Del

# PuTTY sends Ctrl with Left and Right as the arrows in normal cursor mode.
Ctrl-Left       \e[D        Left
Ctrl-Right      \e[C        Right

# rxvt and PuTTY write Alt as an ESC in front of the key's own sequence, which is
# also Escape and then the key pressed quickly — or two keys sent in one packet
# over ssh. Deliberately read as the two keys: see "Alt+Delete and Ctrl+Delete"
# in AGENTS.md.
Alt-Up          \e\e[A      Esc Up
Alt-Down        \e\e[B      Esc Down
Alt-Right       \e\e[C      Esc Right
Alt-Left        \e\e[D      Esc Left
Alt-Up          \e\eOA      Esc Up
Alt-Down        \e\eOB      Esc Down
Alt-Right       \e\eOC      Esc Right
Alt-Left        \e\eOD      Esc Left
Alt-Del         \e\e[3~     Esc Del
Alt-F1          \e\e[11~    Esc F1
Alt-F2          \e\e[12~    Esc F2
Alt-F3          \e\e[13~    Esc F3
Alt-F4          \e\e[14~    Esc F4
Alt-F5          \e\e[15~    Esc F5
Alt-F6          \e\e[17~    Esc F6
Alt-F7          \e\e[18~    Esc F7
Alt-F8          \e\e[19~    Esc F8
Alt-F9          \e\e[20~    Esc F9
Alt-F10         \e\e[21~    Esc F10
Alt-F11         \e\e[23~    Esc F11
Alt-F12         \e\e[24~    Esc F12
